Under `--modular-termination` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211), any trait may now be extended from any module, without `{:termination false}` or `@AssumeCrossModuleTermination`. A member with a `decreases {:global}` bound binds every implementation. A foreign implementation of a member without one must be a leaf: it reaches no dispatched call and no application of a function value whose code is not known, and it cannot declare a bound. A dispatched call to such a member is TOP, so only a member without a bound may make it. The new attribute `{:termination_leaf}` marks an explicit leaf, whose bound is BOTTOM. The legacy forms keep their unchecked meaning for members without a bound. Without the option, nothing changes. The bound check applies to every call, including calls of extreme and prefix predicates and co-calls, and a least or greatest lemma's body runs under the lemma's bound.
